WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.520
Polish has no articles. Why there is no word for a, an or the, and what to do about it.

2
00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:18.150
Polish has no articles: there are no separate words for a, an or the.

3
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:26.260
A bare noun can therefore mean a cat or the cat, and the meaning comes from the situation.

4
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:33.730
When you translate into English, choose a, an or the from the context.

5
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.120
Mam kota.

6
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.960
Mam kota.

7
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:43.360
It means: I have a cat.

8
00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:54.310
There is no word for a. The ending of kota changes because it is the object of the verb; that is a later topic.

9
00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:58.100
Kot śpi.

10
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.340
Kot śpi.

11
00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.900
It means: The cat is sleeping.

12
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:10.450
It could also mean A cat is sleeping, depending on the situation.

13
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.560
Mam psa.

14
00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.120
Mam psa.

15
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.160
It means: I have a dog.

16
00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.190
Let's recap.

17
00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.180
Mam kota.

18
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.820
Kot śpi.

19
00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.780
Mam psa.

20
00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.860
